IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`

-- ind-a-tests-fixtures.l4: shared case values for the independent tests of ind-a (Articles 1 to 12).
-- The expected answers are in the test modules and come from WORK/ind-a/expectations.md, written from the Law before any encoding module was opened.
-- This module holds only facts: who the bodies are, as a witness would state them. No assertion lives here.

§ `ind-a fixtures`

§§ `The facts of Article 2(1), as flags`

-- One flag per witness fact of the G1 record `Facts about the body under Article 2`, so that a body is stated as the list of facts true of it.
DECLARE `ind-a fact` IS ONE OF
    `ind-a trustees of a trust`
    `ind-a fideicommissaires of a court-approved fideicommis`
    `ind-a body corporate`
    `ind-a NPO`
    `ind-a established under Jersey law`
    `ind-a incorporated 1862 association`
    `ind-a Jersey foundation`
    `ind-a established by an enactment`
    `ind-a established by Act of the States`
    `ind-a established by Royal Charter`
    `ind-a established in relation to Jersey`
    `ind-a Jersey company`
    `ind-a incorporated under another Jersey enactment`
    `ind-a incorporated under a UK Act extended to Jersey`
    `ind-a unincorporated association`
    `ind-a partnership`
    `ind-a established under foreign law`
    `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`

GIVEN flags IS A LIST OF `ind-a fact`
      similar IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      lawBy IS A MAYBE STRING
      lawUnder IS A MAYBE STRING
      govs IS A LIST OF Governor
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`ind-a body with` flags similar lawBy lawUnder govs MEANS
    `Facts about the body under Article 2` WITH
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust` IS elem `ind-a trustees of a trust` flags
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` IS elem `ind-a fideicommissaires of a court-approved fideicommis` flags
        `a body corporate` IS elem `ind-a body corporate` flags
        `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS elem `ind-a NPO` flags
        `established under the law of Jersey` IS elem `ind-a established under Jersey law` flags
        `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862` IS elem `ind-a incorporated 1862 association` flags
        `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009` IS elem `ind-a Jersey foundation` flags
        `established by an enactment` IS elem `ind-a established by an enactment` flags
        `established by Act of the States` IS elem `ind-a established by Act of the States` flags
        `established by Royal Charter` IS elem `ind-a established by Royal Charter` flags
        `established in relation to Jersey` IS elem `ind-a established in relation to Jersey` flags
        `the Law by which the body corporate was established` IS lawBy
        `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS elem `ind-a Jersey company` flags
        `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS elem `ind-a incorporated under another Jersey enactment` flags
        `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey` IS elem `ind-a incorporated under a UK Act extended to Jersey` flags
        `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` IS lawUnder
        `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons` IS elem `ind-a unincorporated association` flags
        `a partnership` IS elem `ind-a partnership` flags
        `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to` IS similar
        `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS elem `ind-a established under foreign law` flags
        `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey` IS elem `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law` flags
        `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls` IS EMPTY
        governors IS govs

§§ `Governors`

-- A natural person resident in Jersey.
`ind-a Jersey resident individual` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Ann Le Brun"
        `is a natural person` IS TRUE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

-- A natural person resident in Guernsey.
`ind-a Guernsey resident individual` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Guy Mauger"
        `is a natural person` IS TRUE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

-- A Jersey company acting as a governor: a Jersey entity by Article 2(3)(a), since a company is within 2(1)(f).
`ind-a Jersey company as governor` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Trustco (Jersey) Limited"
        `is a natural person` IS FALSE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS TRUE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

-- Another unincorporated association that is a Jersey entity only by Article 2(3)(b), not by 2(3)(a).
`ind-a association that is a Jersey entity only by 2(3)(b)` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "St Helier Friends Association"
        `is a natural person` IS FALSE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

-- An English company acting as a governor: within 2(1)(j), so not a Jersey entity by 2(3)(a).
`ind-a English company as governor` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Albion Trustees Ltd"
        `is a natural person` IS FALSE
        `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

§§ `Bodies under Article 2(1)`

-- (a) the trustees of a Jersey trust (two individual trustees).
`ind-a trustees of a Jersey trust` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a trustees of a trust`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (b) the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis.
`ind-a fideicommissaires` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a fideicommissaires of a court-approved fideicommis`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (ba) a Jersey NPO body corporate within none of (c) to (h).
`ind-a Jersey NPO body corporate` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a NPO`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

-- (ba) fails (i): a Jersey body corporate within none of (c) to (h) that is not an NPO.
`ind-a Jersey non-NPO body corporate` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

-- (ba) fails (ii): a Guernsey NPO body corporate, within none of (c) to (h), not said to be similar to anything.
`ind-a Guernsey NPO body corporate` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a NPO`, `ind-a established under foreign law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

-- (ba) fails (iii): an NPO that is a Jersey company.
`ind-a Jersey company that is an NPO` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a NPO`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a Jersey company`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (c) an incorporated 1862 association: as written it is also incorporated under an enactment other than the Companies Law (the Loi of 1862).
`ind-a 1862 association` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a incorporated 1862 association`, `ind-a incorporated under another Jersey enactment`) EMPTY NOTHING (JUST "Loi (1862) sur les teneures en fidéicommis et l’incorporation d’associations") EMPTY

-- (d) a Jersey foundation: incorporated under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009, an enactment other than the Companies Law.
`ind-a Jersey foundation body` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a Jersey foundation`, `ind-a incorporated under another Jersey enactment`) EMPTY NOTHING (JUST "Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009") EMPTY

-- (e)(i) a body corporate established by a Jersey Law.
`ind-a body established by a Law` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a established by an enactment`, `ind-a established in relation to Jersey`) EMPTY (JUST "Jersey Heritage (Jersey) Law 2099") NOTHING EMPTY

-- (e)(ii) a body corporate established by Act of the States.
`ind-a body established by Act of the States` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a established by Act of the States`, `ind-a established in relation to Jersey`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

-- (e)(iii) a body corporate established by Royal Charter in relation to Jersey.
`ind-a body established by Royal Charter for Jersey` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established by Royal Charter`, `ind-a established in relation to Jersey`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

-- (f) a Jersey company.
`ind-a Jersey company body` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a Jersey company`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (g) a limited liability company incorporated under a Jersey LLC Law (not the Companies Law).
`ind-a Jersey LLC` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a incorporated under another Jersey enactment`) EMPTY NOTHING (JUST "Limited Liability Companies (Jersey) Law 2018") EMPTY

-- (h) a body incorporated under, not by, a UK Act extended to Jersey.
`ind-a body under a UK Act` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a incorporated under a UK Act extended to Jersey`) EMPTY NOTHING (JUST "Industrial and Provident Societies Act (extended)") EMPTY

-- (i) a Jersey-law unincorporated association with one governor resident in Jersey.
`ind-a Jersey association with a resident governor` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Guernsey resident individual`, `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (i) a Jersey-law association whose only governor is a Jersey company.
`ind-a Jersey association with a company governor` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey company as governor`)

-- (i) a Jersey-law association whose only governor is another association that is a Jersey entity only by 2(3)(b).
`ind-a Jersey association with an association governor` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a association that is a Jersey entity only by 2(3)(b)`)

-- (i) an English-law association with a governor resident in Jersey.
`ind-a English-law association with a resident governor` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (i) a Jersey-law association whose governors all live in Guernsey.
`ind-a Jersey association with Guernsey governors` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Guernsey resident individual`)

-- (i) a Jersey-law association whose only governor is an English company.
`ind-a Jersey association with an English company governor` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a English company as governor`)

-- An unincorporated partnership.
`ind-a partnership body` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a partnership`, `ind-a relationship governed by Jersey law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- (j) an English charitable company, substantially similar to a Jersey company.
`ind-a English charitable company` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under foreign law`) (LIST `a company`) NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- A French unincorporated association (no jurisdiction condition in (i)).
`ind-a French association` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a unincorporated association`, `ind-a established under foreign law`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Guernsey resident individual`)

-- A Jersey company that is the sole trustee of a charitable trust: (a) and (f).
`ind-a Jersey company as sole trustee` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` (LIST `ind-a trustees of a trust`, `ind-a body corporate`, `ind-a established under Jersey law`, `ind-a Jersey company`) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`)

-- A natural person acting alone, not a trustee: no fact of Article 2(1).
`ind-a lone individual` MEANS
    `ind-a body with` EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

§§ `Entities as the later Articles take them (domain Entity)`

GIVEN nm IS A STRING
      st IS A `Standing on the register`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      je IS A BOOLEAN
      gs IS A LIST OF Governor
      ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-a entity` nm st ks je gs ps MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS nm
        `standing on the register` IS st
        `kinds of entity` IS ks
        `is a Jersey entity` IS je
        governors IS gs
        purposes IS ps

-- A purpose recorded under a head, with no flags.
GIVEN d IS A STRING
      h IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A Purpose
`ind-a purpose under` d h MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS d
        head IS JUST h
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

`ind-a relief of poverty purpose` MEANS `ind-a purpose under` "running a food bank for people in poverty" `the prevention or relief of poverty`
`ind-a education purpose` MEANS `ind-a purpose under` "running a school" `the advancement of education`

-- A non-charitable purpose under no head, not ancillary.
`ind-a private business purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS "the benefit of the founder's trading company"
        head IS NOTHING
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- A purely ancillary fundraising-trading purpose under no head.
`ind-a ancillary trading purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS "operating a charity shop to raise funds"
        head IS NOTHING
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- Advancing a political party, put forward as ancillary.
`ind-a political party purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS "supporting the Jersey Progress Party at elections"
        head IS NOTHING
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- Educating voters to support one party: on its face (b), but 6(5) overrides.
`ind-a party education purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS "educating voters about the merits of one party's programme"
        head IS JUST `the advancement of education`
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- Humanism: a philosophical belief not involving a god, recorded under no head.
`ind-a humanism purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH
        description IS "the advancement of humanism"
        head IS NOTHING
        `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
        `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE

-- A Jersey company registered in the general section, with two charitable purposes.
`ind-a general-section company` MEANS
    `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`, `ind-a education purpose`)
